# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# REPO: cloud (PUBLIC)
# https://github.com/diegonmarcos/cloud-infra
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Secrets & Credentials (reinforces global gitignore) ──
# KEEP IN SYNC WITH:
#   Pre-commit hook: 0_git/src/hooks/pre-commit  (blocks even git add -f)
#   Global gitignore: ~/git/cloud-infra-desktop/ba_flakes_desktop/src/modules/programs/git.nix
#   Global gitignore: ~/git/cloud-infra-desktop/bb_flakes_termux/src/modules/programs/git.nix
## Decrypted secrets output
.secrets
*.secrets
**/.secrets
.secrets.d/
**/.secrets.d/
## .secrets.json — JSON dumps of decrypted env (build engine output).
## NOT matched by *.secrets glob (which only matches files literally
## ending in .secrets, not .secrets.json). Found 2026-05-05 leaking
## AUTHELIA_CLI_SECRET / CF_API_TOKEN / NTFY_ADMIN_AUTH from dist/.
.secrets.json
*.secrets.json
**/.secrets.json
**/dist/.secrets.json
## NOTE: secrets.yaml (+ .new / .draft / .bak variants) are ALLOWED
## to be tracked — but ONLY when sops-encrypted. The pre-commit hook's
## content-scan blocks any secret-named file lacking `ENC[AES...]` or
## `sops:` markers. Fix workflow: sops -e -i secrets.yaml → commit OK.
## Environment files
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
## Private keys & certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
## Auth tokens & credentials
*.token
*credentials*.json
*_token.json
*_tokens.json
## Cloud provider configs
.oci/
.gcloud/
## GPG & age
*.asc
*.age
!*.age.pub
## Terraform secrets
terraform.tfvars
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

# ── Dependencies (managed by shared ~/.node_modules) ──
node_modules

# ── Repo-specific ──
## Terraform
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
!*.tfstate.enc
## Nix build artifacts
## Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `result` matches ANY directory of
## that name at any depth, which silently swallowed the 5 tracked C++ sources
## in ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/keyboard/.../suggest/core/result/.
/result
/.result
## Temporary files
*.tmp
## Generated data files → symlinks to cloud-data/ submodule (tracked)
## Obsidian
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# Deployed secrets (never commit)
b_infra/nixhm-sudo-*/dist/.secrets
b_infra/nixhm-sudo-*/dist/.secrets.d/

# ── Nix closure binaries (generated by HM docker-package step) ──
*.nar.gz
**/nix-store/
**/nix-path-info.json.gz

# ── Vendored Python deps (regenerated at build time) ──
**/.deps/

# ── Rust build artifacts (regenerated at build time) ──
**/target/
**/.cargo-home/

## Per-service build transcript written by cloud-ship-container-engine.sh
## (tee -a "$BUILD_LOG_FILE"). Purely local run output — 65 of these staged
## themselves the first time every service build.sh was exercised.
build.log
**/build.log

# ── Agent/editor machine state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
## These sit inside directories that ARE committed (.claude/, .obsidian/), so
## they need naming individually — the deploy step already treats them as
## "machine state, never managed" and refuses to overwrite them, but nothing
## stopped them being committed. vault and tools each shipped a
## settings.local.json full of one machine's Bash permission grants, including
## absolute paths into a repo layout that no longer exists.
##
## Committed alongside, deliberately: .claude/settings.json (shared config) and
## .mcp.json (generated, identical everywhere).
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude.json
.claude.json.backup
.claude.json.tmp.*
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

## ─── Android app trees (moved from cloud-infra-desktop 2026-08-25, ea_* -> aa_* (superapp) / ab_* (libs) / ac_* (apps)) ───
## EXCEPTION: ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/ is THE gradle multi-module source tree
## for every shared library. All 30 modules were consolidated here 2026-08-30
## from aa_cloud-superapp/libs/ (which no longer exists) - the negation moved
## with them, because a negation pointing at a vanished directory silently
## stops protecting anything. Seventh time this blanket rule has needed one.
!ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/
!ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/**
## EXCEPTION: ac_cloud-wallet/libs/ is the gradle multi-module source tree
## (libs:wallet). Same pattern as aa_cloud-superapp/libs/. Added 2026-07-12.
!ac_cloud-wallet/libs/
!ac_cloud-wallet/libs/**
## EXCEPTION: ac_cloud-nav/libs/ is the gradle multi-module source tree
## (libs:core, libs:maps, libs:updater). Same pattern as aa_cloud-superapp/libs/.
!ac_cloud-nav/libs/
!ac_cloud-nav/libs/**
## EXCEPTION: ac_cloud-calendar/libs/ is the gradle multi-module source tree
## (libs:core, libs:updater, libs:cal). Same pattern as aa_cloud-superapp/libs/.
!ac_cloud-calendar/libs/
!ac_cloud-calendar/libs/**
## EXCEPTION: ac_cloud-news/libs/ is the gradle multi-module source tree
!ac_cloud-news/libs/
!ac_cloud-news/libs/**
!ac_cloud-contacts/libs/
!ac_cloud-contacts/libs/**
## EXCEPTION: ac_cloud-vault/libs/ — the FIFTH time this blanket rule has
!ac_cloud-vault/libs/
!ac_cloud-vault/libs/**
## EXCEPTION: ac_cloud-media-center/libs/ — the SIXTH time. Path updated when
## upstream/ was flattened to the app root (2026-08-29): the old
## !ac_cloud-media-center/upstream/libs/ stopped matching after the move, which
## would have let the blanket libs/ rule swallow 68 tracked files on the next
## git add — silently, because git add never reports what it ignored. This one
## as !ac_cloud-media-center/libs/ would not have matched it.
!ac_cloud-media-center/libs/
!ac_cloud-media-center/libs/**
aa_cloud-superapp/**/*.keystore
aa_cloud-superapp/**/*.jks
ea_cloud-comms/**/*.keystore
ea_cloud-comms/**/*.jks
ac_cloud-ide/**/*.keystore
ac_cloud-ide/**/*.jks
ac_cloud-nav/**/*.keystore
ac_cloud-nav/**/*.jks
## Bitwarden Android for ac_cloud-vault's `vault-bitwarden` fork, added
## ac_cloud-<app>/patches/ (tracked). Was covered by the old `ea_*-*/`
## ac_upstreams-sources/ was deleted 2026-08-30: every fork is now vendored
## in-repo (tracker_dir points at the app's own tree), so there is no external
## clone workspace left to ignore. Kept as a note rather than silence, because
## the rule's absence is what a future "why is my upstream clone tracked?"
## question will look for.
ac_cloud-wallet/**/*.keystore
ac_cloud-wallet/**/*.jks
ac_cloud-me/**/*.keystore
ac_cloud-me/**/*.jks
ac_cloud-browser/**/*.keystore
ac_cloud-browser/**/*.jks
ac_cloud-vault/**/*.keystore
ac_cloud-vault/**/*.jks
ac_cloud-contacts/**/*.keystore
ac_cloud-contacts/**/*.jks
ac_cloud-media-center/**/*.keystore
ac_cloud-media-center/**/*.jks
## `ea_*-*/` blanket rule removed 2026-07-10; 93fdc30c re-added explicit ignores
## that were later lost. If any becomes a real app, whitelist it like ac_cloud-*.
ac_keyboard-dicts/
ac_keyboard-heliboard/
## firestack moved INTO the module that consumes it
## (ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/firewall/firestack) and is committed there,
## so the old gitignored root clone no longer exists. What stays ignored is
## its BUILD OUTPUT: upstream's own bin/ (24 MB, untracked upstream too) and
## the gomobile work dir. The produced firestack.aar is ignored separately
## below, next to the module it lands in.
ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/firewall/firestack/bin/
ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/firewall/firestack/build/
## The built aar lands in the same folder as the source it is built from (that
## is the path lib-apks/settings.gradle's flatDir already resolves), so it has
## to be ignored by name or `git add -A` would commit a ~20 MB build artifact.
ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/firewall/firestack/*.aar
ac_zoomies-pets/
ac_mail-fairmail/
ac_cal-davx5/
ac_feed-feeder/
ac_net-wireguard/
ac_vault-keepassdx/
ac_net-kdeconnect/
ac_net-rethinkdns/
## Re-ignore Gradle build outputs inside the whitelisted ac_cloud-ide/ tree
## (the !ac_cloud-ide/** whitelist would otherwise track build/.gradle dirs).
ac_cloud-ide/.gradle/
ac_cloud-ide/build/
ac_cloud-ide/**/build/
ac_cloud-nav/.gradle/
ac_cloud-nav/build/
ac_cloud-nav/**/build/
ac_cloud-media-center/.gradle/
ac_cloud-media-center/build/
ac_cloud-media-center/**/build/
## ac_cloud-calendar was added after this list and never got its entries, so a
## ~3M-line aa_cloud-superapp cache commit (264c09f2). Added 2026-08-09.
ac_cloud-calendar/.gradle/
ac_cloud-calendar/build/
ac_cloud-calendar/**/build/
ac_cloud-calendar/.cache/
ac_cloud-calendar/.kotlin/
## Same for ac_cloud-news. These MUST sort after the !ac_cloud-news/libs/**
ac_cloud-news/.gradle/
ac_cloud-news/build/
ac_cloud-news/**/build/
## Same for ac_cloud-vault — MUST sort after its whitelist above.
ac_cloud-vault/.gradle/
ac_cloud-vault/build/
ac_cloud-vault/**/build/
ac_cloud-vault/.cache/
ac_cloud-vault/.kotlin/
ac_cloud-news/.cache/
ac_cloud-news/.kotlin/
ac_cloud-contacts/.gradle/
ac_cloud-contacts/build/
ac_cloud-contacts/**/build/
ac_cloud-contacts/.cache/
ac_cloud-contacts/.kotlin/
## Same for ab_cloud-libs-shared — MUST sort after its whitelist above. The
## !ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/** negation un-ignores EVERYTHING beneath it,
## build/ and .cxx/ included, so without these `git add -A` stages 32,128
## generated files: libs/net vendors a whole Go source tree under
## build/intermediates/cxx/. Same class as the ~3M-line commit 264c09f2, and
## the reason that one happened is that a repo was added to the whitelist and
## never to this list. Added 2026-08-30 with the shared-module consolidation.
ab_cloud-libs-shared/.gradle/
ab_cloud-libs-shared/build/
ab_cloud-libs-shared/**/build/
ab_cloud-libs-shared/**/.cxx/
ab_cloud-libs-shared/.cache/
ab_cloud-libs-shared/.kotlin/
## ac_cloud-calendar's first local ./gradlew run surfaced it, but the gap
## Re-ignore Gradle/Kotlin daemon caches inside the whitelisted aa_cloud-superapp/
aa_cloud-superapp/.cache/
aa_cloud-superapp/.kotlin/
## !ea_cloud-*/** whitelists would otherwise make a locally-built APK / dist/
aa_cloud-superapp/dist/
aa_cloud-superapp/**/*.apk
ea_cloud-comms/dist/
ea_cloud-comms/**/*.apk
ac_cloud-ide/dist/
ac_cloud-ide/**/*.apk
ac_cloud-nav/dist/
ac_cloud-nav/**/*.apk
ac_cloud-wallet/dist/
ac_cloud-wallet/**/*.apk
ac_cloud-browser/dist/
ac_cloud-browser/**/*.apk
