ac_cloud-media-center/**/*.apk
ac_cloud-calendar/dist/
ac_cloud-calendar/**/*.apk
## ae-tool_termux-boot + c_devices/garmin-watchface arrived from cloud-infra-desktop
## (2026-08-27). Termux Boot is Gradle like the ac_cloud-* apps, so it needs the
## same build-output rules; *.jks/*.keystore are already global above.
a_solutions/ae-tool_termux-boot/.gradle/
a_solutions/ae-tool_termux-boot/build/
a_solutions/ae-tool_termux-boot/**/build/
a_solutions/ae-tool_termux-boot/local.properties
## Garmin is monkeyc, not Gradle: build.sh writes dist/ (incl. the developer key,
## which must never be vendored) per design.
c_devices/garmin-watchface/dist/

## Fetched at build time, never committed: the watchdog sampler + panel
## (multi-MB static musl binaries) and the UI shell the panel generates. All
## three come from the my-watchdog rolling release, so committing them would
## vendor a build artifact that the release already versions.
ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/watchdog/src/main/jniLibs/
ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/watchdog/src/main/assets/watchdog-app.html
ac_cloud-termux/app/src/main/jniLibs/
ac_cloud-nix-on-droid/app/src/main/jniLibs/

## The release keystore the fork engine copies in (signing=vault_jks_env).
## *.jks is already ignored globally; named here so it is obvious why the path
## exists in a build and never in the tree.
ac_cloud-termux/app/release.jks
ac_cloud-nix-on-droid/app/release.jks

## Tracked here on purpose; overrides the global core.excludesFile `.vscode/`.
!.vscode/
